    "c2": {
      "anchor": "p-mermaid-drawings#field-2",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Mermaid Drawings",
      "excerpt": "Your words (Owen, 2026-11-18): \"new spell-ui component: `mermaid` drawing which",
      "text": "I'm going to want ELK for the new ui-diagram component",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-19T01:42:18.369Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "12.0 ELK is built into",
      "offset": 5024,
      "edited": "2026-11-19T01:42:28.615Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-19T02:35:13.442Z",
          "html": "<p>ELK is now one shared, lazily loaded engine in P37 (<a href=\"#q56\">Q56</a>).</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Mermaid 12.3's npm module doesn't copy ELK in: it imports <code>elkjs</code> lazily, as an ordinary dependency.</li>\n  <li>One loader, <code>ElkEngine</code>, imports the same file, so the build has one ELK chunk, loaded once per page.</li>\n  <li><code>&lt;ui-diagram&gt;</code> using it is todo <a href=\"#t115\">T115</a>, not queued.</li>\n</ul>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c3": {
      "anchor": "q60",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "Where should a view on its own open?",
      "excerpt": "Where should a view on its own open?",
      "text": "Maybe this is a separate \"design\" view in the toolbar `run|edit|design|site` where I can choose what I want to tweak and do the layout.  Code sidebar hidden, instead we'd have a left sidebar to pull out components so we don't have the dropdown.  Can still have the right sidebar to see properties of the inspected view in this mode, and right code pane, the `views` pane would show just the components in the view that I'm editing.",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-20T00:45:19.681Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-20T00:52:35.127Z",
          "html": "<p>Taken as you said it:  Design becomes its own mode in the top bar, Run | Edit | Design | Site (Site still only for a site).</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><a href=\"#q60\">Q60</a> is decided that way, and the Card alone button goes.</li>\n  <li>\n    <a href=\"#p-view-on-its-own\">P37 · Design Mode</a>:  the Design tab, a picker of what to tweak (each draw method,\n    the property editor, a site's pages), a large canvas to drag parts into, and the property editor as a form.\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <a href=\"#p-side-by-side-and-sizes\">P38 · Side By Side And Sizes</a>:  the sheet of samples with Save, and phone /\n    tablet / desktop frames.\n  </li>\n  <li>Open questions:  <a href=\"#q61\">Q61</a>-<a href=\"#q65\">Q65</a>.</li>\n</ul>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-20T00:49:04.217Z"
      }
    }
  },
